# Technical Stack

Frontend:

 - React (TypeScript) + Vite 
 - Tailwind CSS for styling
 - WebSocket client (like Socket.io-client) for real-time chat
 - React Query/SWR for data fetching and caching

Backend:

 - Node.js with Express/NestJS for API server
 - WebSocket server (Socket.io) for real-time chat

 - MongoDB for primary database
  - Store user accounts, events, chat messages
  - Better for relational data like event attendees, group memberships

 - Redis for:
  - Session management
  - Real-time chat message caching
  - Pub/Sub for WebSocket scaling

 - Infrastructure:
  - Docker for containerization
  - Hostinger for hosting
  - Nginx as reverse proxy
  - CI/CD pipeline (GitHub Actions/GitLab CI)
 
 - Security:
  - JWT for authentication
  - HTTPS for all connections
  - Rate limiting for API endpoints
  - Input validation and sanitization
